## What I learned

- `requests` are used by the Kubernetes scheduler to decide whether a Pod can fit on a node.
- `limits` define the upper boundary of runtime resource consumption.
- Exceeding a memory limit can cause container termination with `OOMKilled`.
- CPU overuse usually results in throttling instead of process termination.
- A Pod can be healthy at startup but still fail later under resource pressure.
- Stress endpoints inside the application make resource behavior much easier to observe and understand.
